 "preferred_name": "Market depth",
 "kind": "knowledge",
 "definition": "A measure of how many buy and sell orders sit at different prices, showing how large a trade a market can absorb without the price moving much.",
 "description": {
  "text": "In finance, market depth is a real-time list showing the quantity for sale at each price, organized by price level. Mathematically it is the order size needed to move the market price by a given amount; in a deep market, a large order is needed.",
